---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="AI Hardware Campaign — Local AI for Community Help | Base Impact"
  description="Base Impact is seeking AI-capable laptops, workstations, and servers with 32–128 GB unified memory for form filling, research, and nonprofit technology support in Brevard, Volusia, and Orange counties, Florida."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="picture-band -mx-4 sm:-mx-0">
      <img
        src="/assets/laptop-neat-desk.jpg"
        alt="A laptop beside a desktop computer on a desk — illustrative photo of the type of equipment Base Impact is seeking"
        width="1920"
        height="1280"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow tracking-widest mt-6">Campaign · Local AI infrastructure</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold text-body mt-2 mb-4 max-w-3xl fade-in">
      Local AI, in the hands of the people who help.
    </h1>
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-muted leading-relaxed text-lg fade-in">
      Base Impact is raising AI-capable computers so volunteers can sit with a neighbor and fill out a
      housing or benefits form, research what help is available, and build or repair websites for small
      nonprofits. The work stays on the machine, not in someone else's cloud account.
    </p>

    <section class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 mt-8 fade-in" aria-label="The hardware ask at a glance">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-5 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <p class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-body">32–128 GB</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Unified memory, from workable minimum to ideal</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-5 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <p class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-body">3 paths</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Portable laptop, office workstation, or shared server</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-5 shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
        <p class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-body">Local first</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Client documents stay on hardware we control</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 pt-10 fade-in">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-1">The need</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">What a machine like this does here</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-lead">
          This is not AI for its own sake. Each use case starts with a neighbor or a small nonprofit
          that already has a problem, and a volunteer who needs better tools to solve it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:gap-6">
        <article class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Forms, with a person beside you</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Housing applications, benefits renewals, and job forms are long and full of acronyms.
            A local assistant reads the questions out loud, explains what each one means, and helps
            draft answers. A volunteer reviews everything and the neighbor decides what to submit.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Finding and researching help</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            "Who can help with rent this week?" is a research question. We want to answer it from
            verified local sources, with links a neighbor can open later, instead of sending someone
            away with a generic chat response.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Websites for small nonprofits</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            A pantry or church may need a page that lists hours, a donation form, or an event calendar.
            Local AI helps a volunteer write, edit, and debug the site faster, so a 1–5 person group
            gets a usable web presence without hiring an agency.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Edits and plain-language writing</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Grant narratives, flyers, intake scripts, and text for a shelter's website all need clear
            wording. The machine does the first pass locally; our volunteers and partner staff make
            the final call.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Custom tools for real workflows</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Some problems need a small script, not another subscription: a form checker, a document
            sorter, a batch of label prints. A local machine lets us build and test that software in
            the same room as the people who will use it.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">One shared office inference box</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            A workstation or server at the office can serve several volunteers over our own network.
            That is cheaper than a per-seat cloud bill and keeps sensitive files inside the building.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 pt-10 fade-in">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-1">The ask</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Equipment we can put to work</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-lead">
          We are flexible on brand and form factor. What matters is enough memory to hold a local
          model, enough storage for documents, and hardware we can keep secure and updated.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line" style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table class="w-full text-sm text-left" style="min-width: 680px;">
          <caption class="sr-only">AI hardware needs by form factor</caption>
          <thead class="bg-band">
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-body">Form factor</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-body">Target specification</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-body">How we'd use it</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-t border-line align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold text-body">Portable laptop</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                32 GB unified memory minimum, 64–128 GB preferred; 1 TB SSD or larger;
                modern CPU/GPU/NPU; all-day battery; serviceable and under warranty if possible
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                Home visits, shelter sites, and partner offices. The assistant travels to the neighbor.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-line align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold text-body">Office workstation</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                64–128 GB unified or high-bandwidth memory; 2 TB SSD; discrete or integrated AI
                accelerator; reliable cooling; UPS or surge protection
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                Document processing, web builds, and custom code. Also a backup for the laptops.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-line align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold text-body">Server / inference node</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                128 GB+ system memory or 48 GB+ VRAM per GPU; 2 TB+ SSD; remote access over our own
                VPN; power, cooling, and physical security at the office
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                Shared local inference for several volunteers, with central updates and access control.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-line align-top">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold text-body">Supporting gear</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                Docks, external SSDs, labels, surge protectors, UPS units, and network gear
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-4 text-muted">
                Keeps donated machines usable, identifiable, and safe to leave with a partner.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mt-4 max-w-3xl">
        For scale, current shipping examples of this class include the
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/macbook-pro/liquid-retina-xdr-display/specs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">MacBook Pro specs</a>,
        where M5 Max configurations offer up to 128 GB of unified memory, and systems built on the
        <a href="https://www.amd.com/en/products/processors/laptop/ryzen/ai-300-series/amd-ryzen-ai-max-plus-395.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395</a>,
        which supports up to 128 GB. We do not require either platform. These are reference points,
        checked 2026-11-27, not a preferred-vendor list.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        We also welcome refurbished business machines, returned or open-box units, and older
        equipment that still meets the memory floor. If you are unsure whether your system fits,
        <a href="/contact" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">send us the specs</a>
        and we will give you a straight answer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 pt-10 fade-in">
      <h2 class="section-title mb-4">Why local changes the service</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Privacy by design</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            A neighbor's ID, income details, and address do not become somebody else's training data.
            Assisted sessions happen on hardware we control, with a volunteer in the room.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Works when the connection doesn't</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Shelters and rural partner sites have unreliable internet. A local model keeps helping
            when the hotspot drops, and it does not stop for a subscription renewal.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">A human stays responsible</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            The assistant suggests. The volunteer checks. The neighbor decides. We do not automate
            submissions or give AI the last word on anyone's benefits or housing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-card p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Capacity that compounds</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            One good machine can serve many partners. The tools we build with it can be shared
            with other small nonprofits, so the value of a single gift keeps growing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 pt-10 fade-in">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-1">Stewardship</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">What happens to a donated device</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-lead">
          We treat hardware donations as assets with a chain of custody, not as anonymous gifts.
          Here is the path from your shipment to a neighbor's hands.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
        <li class="lp-card p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-accent">01 · Receive</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Log serial number, source, and condition. Photograph the item before setup.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="lp-card p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-accent">02 · Sanitize</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Wipe and reinstall before any reuse. Refurbished units get a documented check.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="lp-card p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-accent">03 · Deploy</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Asset tag, install local model tools, set updates, access controls, and backups.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="lp-card p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-accent">04 · Report</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Track sessions and outcomes by site, and share a report with the donor.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="lp-card p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-accent">05 · Retire</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Reuse within the program first, then wipe and recycle through a responsible outlet.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mt-4 max-w-3xl">
        We do not publish recipient names, addresses, or identifying documents. Photos and stories
        are used only with consent, and a donor may choose to stay unnamed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 pt-10 fade-in">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-band border border-line p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">For manufacturers, distributors &amp; corporate donors</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-body">Bring your product to a working pilot</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
          We are approaching hardware makers, distributors, and large companies now. If you have a
          product that fits, tell us the model and specs. We will write the spec, confirm quantities,
          and report back what shipped and how it was used. We are equally glad to discuss nonprofit
          pricing, refurbished or returned stock, warranty coverage, engineering time, or training
          for our volunteers.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mt-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-body">A donation can look like</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-muted mt-2 space-y-1">
              <li>One or more laptops with 64–128 GB unified memory</li>
              <li>A desk-side workstation or rack/tower inference server</li>
              <li>Current-generation or open-box systems under warranty</li>
              <li>Docks, storage, UPS units, and network gear</li>
              <li>Grants or funds that let us buy the missing piece</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-body">What we provide in return</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-muted mt-2 space-y-1">
              <li>An itemized intake record and asset tags</li>
              <li>Outcome reports tied to sessions and sites served</li>
              <li>Consented photos and a short case study, if you want one</li>
              <li>Public recognition on this site and in materials, where appropriate</li>
              <li>Our EIN and current nonprofit status documentation for your review</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-full bg-accent px-6 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-accent-hover btn-pill">
            Pitch a product or ask a question
          </a>
          <a href="mailto:grants@baseimpact.org" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-full border border-line px-6 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-body hover:bg-inset btn-pill">
            Email grants@baseimpact.org
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 pt-10 fade-in">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-1">How to help</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Four ways to move this forward</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="/donate" class="lp-card p-6 block hover:bg-inset">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Give funds</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Flexible money lets us buy the exact missing component instead of waiting for a match.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Donate → /donate</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/contact" class="lp-card p-6 block hover:bg-inset">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Offer hardware or expertise</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Use the contact form and mention "AI hardware" with the model, specs, and quantity.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Contact us → /contact</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/grants" class="lp-card p-6 block hover:bg-inset">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Fund it as a grant</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">We can supply budgets, itemized needs, outcome measures, and a partner list on request.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Grants &amp; funding → /grants</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/ai-hardware-campaign" class="lp-card p-6 block hover:bg-inset">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-body">Read the story</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Why we're asking for computers, what "unified memory" means, and what happens next.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Read the article →</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 pt-10 fade-in">
      <h2 class="section-title mb-3">Related work</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2 max-w-3xl">
        <li><a href="/grants/ai-toolkit" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">AI Grant Toolkit</a>: the privacy-first software this hardware will help us build and run.</li>
        <li><a href="/impact" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">Impact</a>: where local AI fits among our programs.</li>
        <li><a href="/partners" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">Partners</a>: the churches, pantries, and outreach groups we build alongside.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 mb-12 rounded-2xl bg-band p-6 border border-line fade-in">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body">Where this stands</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        This campaign opened on 2026-11-27. No hardware has been received through it yet. We are
        publishing the full ask before the first gift arrives so funders and manufacturers can see
        exactly what we plan to do. As machines come in, we will update this page with what arrived,
        where it is deployed, and how it is being used.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Base Impact Inc. is a Florida nonprofit corporation (EIN 43-2200667) with 501(c)(3) status
        pending. Donations are not currently tax-deductible. Please consult your tax advisor.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
        Mims, FL 32754 · <a href="tel:+13213230999" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">(321) 323-0999</a>
        · <a href="mailto:donations@baseimpact.org" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">donations@baseimpact.org</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
